{
 "fps": 30,
 "frames": 1350,
 "dur": 45.0,
 "target": 45.0,
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "Moose delivered nine tons of concrete to Elm Street. In one piece.",
   "s": 0.12,
   "e": 3.519
  },
  {
   "text": "He'd bet Dolores a week of donuts he could get there without turning the drum.",
   "s": 3.719,
   "e": 7.098
  },
  {
   "text": "\"Spinning is for washing machines!\" he said, and flipped it off.",
   "s": 7.298,
   "e": 10.11
  },
  {
   "text": "Bruno the bulldog, who jogs on that drum every morning, slid right off.",
   "s": 10.31,
   "e": 13.625
  },
  {
   "text": "Then eleven ducklings crossed Main Street. Slowly. For two hours.",
   "s": 13.825,
   "e": 17.273
  },
  {
   "text": "Inside the drum, the concrete went soup, oatmeal, peanut butter, bowling ball.",
   "s": 17.473,
   "e": 21.04
  },
  {
   "text": "Moose hit the switch. The drum stayed put. The whole truck spun instead.",
   "s": 21.24,
   "e": 24.476
  },
  {
   "text": "So what turned it to stone in there?",
   "s": 24.676,
   "e": 25.972
  },
  {
   "text": "Concrete doesn't dry. Water and cement grab hands and grow into rock, even underwater.",
   "s": 26.272,
   "e": 30.733
  },
  {
   "text": "Spinning keeps it stirred like a smoothie, so it can't lock up.",
   "s": 31.133,
   "e": 33.878
  },
  {
   "text": "Stop for two hours, and you get a nine-ton gumball.",
   "s": 34.078,
   "e": 36.464
  },
  {
   "text": "\"Spinning is for washing machines,\" Moose whispered. The builders called a crane.",
   "s": 36.664,
   "e": 40.128
  },
  {
   "text": "Dolores got her donuts. Bruno got a nine-ton jogging ball.",
   "s": 40.328,
   "e": 43.521
  }
 ],
